sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The vertebral girder of large animals such as Diplodocus or Stegosaurus is shallower than an engineer's cantilever of comparable load, because a deeper girder would increase rigidity, and an animal's backbone must combine strength with flexibility.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Backbone girders are shallower than engineers would build because flexibility is needed";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XVI, “On Form and Mechanical Efficiency”; topic “Strength versus flexibility of the backbone”. Scope: vertebral columns of large vertebrates"
}
